# .vercelignore — controls what the Vercel CLI uploads on `vercel`/`vercel --prod`.
#
# IMPORTANT: the Vercel CLI does NOT read .gitignore. Anything heavy that lives
# locally must be excluded HERE, or the CLI tries to hash all ~18k files and
# runs out of heap (JS "Reached heap limit" OOM during upload).

# ── Dependencies (Vercel installs these from package.json on build) ──
node_modules

# ── Playwright auto-apply runtime state ──
# Chrome profiles = thousands of tiny files + Unix sockets (SingletonSocket,
# SingletonLock, SingletonCookie) that the CLI can't hash → the OOM trigger.
# They also hold the signed-in browser sessions. The scan, search and JD
# profiles (chrome-scan-profile, …) took the function to 1 GB on 2026-10-18.
scratch
data/chrome-*profile

# Meshy source exports. The site serves the compressed glbs next to this folder.
images/3d/floating-island/source

# Old agence hero renders: gitignored, nothing references them (29 MB).
images/agence-hero.mp4
images/agence-hero-scrub.mp4

# The function caps at 250 MB uncompressed and vercel.json bundles data/**.
# The scan decision log is append-only (the server never reads it, 67 MB),
# and the backups are local safety copies.
data/scan-decisions.jsonl
data/*-backup-*
data/profile-backups

# ── Local-only artifacts not needed by ui/server.mjs ──
reports
outputs
batch
jds
interview-prep
docs

# ── Env / secrets / build + editor state ──
.env
.env.local
.git
.vercel
.DS_Store
.claude

# Unreferenced heavy images (2026-10-21): the function was 252 MB for a 250 MB cap.
# lvmh.webp is the cover in use; the three PNGs are leftovers of old interface covers.
ui/covers/lvmh.jpg
ui/assets/lung-3d.png
ui/assets/doctor-mark.png
ui/assets/opero-platform.png
